From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: surface-laptop8: Add the USB4 P2RR2P pipe
 clock to usb_0_qmpphy

The USB4 part of the QMP combo PHY needs one more GCC clock, the P2RR2P
(PHY-to-Router, Router-to-PHY) pipe clock, enabled before the PHY can be
initialised in USB4 mode. The qmp-combo USB4 support looks it up as
"p2rr2p_pipe" and refuses USB4 mode when it is missing. Hamoa got the
same description in the series that added that driver support:

  https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260908-topic-usb4phy-v5-5-73aac69578ef@oss.qualcomm.com

Add it to usb_0_qmpphy in the Surface Laptop 8 device tree, the only
Glymur PHY that has been run in USB4 mode. The driver enables the clock
only on entry to USB4 mode, so USB3 and DisplayPort operation of the
PHY does not change. The shared glymur.dtsi is left as it is until the
binding allows the clock.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts    | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
index 8820d082745..ebdd491a7a3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
@@ -992,6 +992,18 @@ &usb_0_qmpphy {
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l4h_e0>;
 	refgen-supply = <&vreg_l2f_e0>;
 
+	/* USB4 mode also needs the P2RR2P pipe clock. */
+	clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_AUX_CLK>,
+		 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
+		 <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_COM_AUX_CLK>,
+		 <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_PIPE_CLK>,
+		 <&gcc GCC_USB4_0_PHY_P2RR2P_PIPE_CLK>;
+	clock-names = "aux",
+		      "ref",
+		      "com_aux",
+		      "usb3_pipe",
+		      "p2rr2p_pipe";
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
